{"doc_id": "1611.07438", "page_idx": 0, "element_id": "1611.07438_formula_14", "latex": "\\begin{array}{l} \\Pr (e ^ {+} | c ^ {+}, \\mathbf {b}) \\\\ = \\frac {1}{\\Pr (c ^ {+} , \\mathbf {b})} \\sum_ {\\mathbf {X} ^ {\\prime}, \\mathbf {Y} ^ {\\prime}, \\mathbf {Q} ^ {\\prime}, \\mathbf {Z}} \\Pr (\\mathbf {x}, c ^ {+}, \\mathbf {y}, \\mathbf {q}) \\\\ \\cdot \\Pr (e ^ {+} | \\text {P r i o r} (E)) \\cdot \\Pr (\\mathbf {z} | \\text {P r i o r} (\\mathbf {Z})) \\\\ = \\frac {1}{\\Pr (c ^ {+} , \\mathbf {b})} \\sum_ {\\mathbf {X} ^ {\\prime}, \\mathbf {Y} ^ {\\prime}, \\mathbf {Q} ^ {\\prime}} \\Pr (\\mathbf {x}, c ^ {+}, \\mathbf {y}, \\mathbf {q}) \\cdot \\Pr (e ^ {+} | \\operatorname {P r i o r} (E)). \\\\ \\end{array}"}
